ance.\n</think>"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "link": 17, "label": "text", "type": "STRING"}], "flags": {}, "id": 21, "type": "ShowText|pysssss", "properties": {"Node name for S&R": "ShowText|pysssss"}, "order": 43}, {"mode": 4, "outputs": [{"shape": 6, "name": "STRING", "label": "STRING", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "STRING"}], "size": [315, 112], "pos": [2725.631103515625, 1621.6903076171875], "widgets_values": ["", "<think>\nTo create the desired effect, the original image's characters are transformed into a 3D chibi style, maintaining their proportions and clothing details. The background is replaced with a Polaroid frame, and the characters are positioned as if stepping out of the frame, creating a dynamic visual effect. The hand holding the Polaroid is added to complete the scene.\n</think>"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "link": 23, "label": "text", "type": "STRING"}], "flags": {}, "id": 29, "type": "ShowText|pysssss", "properties": {"Node name for S&R": "ShowText|pysssss"}, "order": 46}, {"mode": 4, "outputs": [{"name": "IMAGE", "links": [2], "label": "IMAGE", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "IMAGE"}, {"name": "MASK", "label": "MASK", "type": "MASK", "localized_name": "MASK"}], "size": [315, 314], "pos": [1369.2823486328125, -284.22998046875], "widgets_values": ["1f8b7814257fd79b18d72a6b62f778679f434b673e97c7fd3a788f11e315d036.png", "image", ""], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "id": 3, "type": "LoadImage", "properties": {"Node name for S&R": "LoadImage"}, "order": 0}, {"mode": 4, "outputs": [{"name": "IMAGE", "links": [29], "label": "IMAGE", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "IMAGE"}, {"name": "MASK", "label": "MASK", "type": "MASK", "localized_name": "MASK"}], "size": [315, 314], "pos": [157.81797790527344, -329.545654296875], "widgets_values": ["d9f8ba67d71d5d7df41790ba2b45f18ecd00883d200107f455b54b5c108cd565.webp", "image", ""], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "id": 15, "type": "LoadImage", "properties": {"Node name for S&R": "LoadImage"}, "order": 1}, {"mode": 4, "outputs": [{"name": "text", "links": [28], "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "size": [400, 204], "pos": [497.0688171386719, -300.0073547363281], "widgets_values": ["What is x in the equation?", false, false, 0.3, 512], "inputs": [{"name": "model", "link": 63, "label": "model", "type": "BAGEL_MODEL", "localized_name": "model"}, {"name": "image", "link": 29, "label": "image", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image"}], "flags": {}, "id": 37, "type": "BagelImageUnderstanding", "properties": {"Node name for S&R": "BagelImageUnderstanding"}, "order": 15}, {"mode": 4, "outputs": [{"shape": 6, "name": "STRING", "label": "STRING", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "STRING"}], "size": [393.8013000488281, 322.27392578125], "pos": [917.0021362304688, -273.98779296875], "widgets_values": ["", "To solve the equation \\((x + 3)^2 = 4\\), we need to take the square root of both sides. Remember that taking the square root of a number gives both a positive and a negative result. So, we have:\n\n\\[\nx + 3 = \\pm 2\n\\]\n\nNow, we solve for \\(x\\) in both cases:\n\n1. When \\(x + 3 = 2\\):\n\\[\nx = 2 - 3 = -1\n\\]\n\n2. When \\(x + 3 = -2\\):\n\\[\nx = -2 - 3 = -5\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the solutions for \\(x\\) are \\(x = -1\\) and \\(x = -5\\)."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "link": 28, "label": "text", "type": "STRING"}], "flags": {}, "id": 38, "type": "ShowText|pysssss", "properties": {"Node name for S&R": "ShowText|pysssss"}, "order": 25}, {"mode": 4, "outputs": [{"name": "text", "links": [3], "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "size": [400, 204], "pos": [1708.9697265625, -283.28076171875], "widgets_values": ["What do you see in this image?", false, false, 0.8000000000000002, 512], "inputs": [{"name": "model", "link": 64, "label": "model", "type": "BAGEL_MODEL", "localized_name": "model"}, {"name": "image", "link": 2, "label